## 1. Corrections to the previous reports

1. The earlier feasibility report said typed was not planned and that A2 had been "discarded". Both are wrong. ADR 0010 recommends A3 and keeps A2 as an alternative that it judged costly (`docs/adr/0010-actor-api.md:54-60`); it never decided Typed semantics. A program already exists: epic #746 (ACT2-PROGRAM), Typed sub-epic #763 (TYP-01 #809 "Specify the Typed Behavior boundary on the shared runtime" through TYP-33) and typed services #764. The recommendation to "postpone typed" is withdrawn.
2. A3 does not prevent porting Typed semantics. A3 fixes the shape of the Go API (`Ref[T]`, `Actor[T]`, `Context[T]`). Typed semantics (default Stop, signals, per-behavior supervision, stash, timers, adapters) are runtime contracts. A `Behavior[T]` API can be a thin layer implemented as an `Actor[T]` over the same runtime, which is what TYP-01 #809 already assumes.
3. Cell counts in the earlier report conflated test and production lines in places; this document uses the per-package counts from section 4.

